# Allowlist for scripts/fips-guard.sh: the known uses of cryptography that is
# not FIPS 140-3 approved, or that fails under GODEBUG=fips140=only.
#
# One entry per line: <path> <rule> <reason>
#   path    the file, relative to the repository root (enterprise/... for the
#           enterprise submodule)
#   rule    an import path (crypto/md5, golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt, ...) or a
#           call (cipher.NewGCM, cipher.NewCFBDecrypter, ...), as the guard
#           reports it
#   reason  one line: why this use exists, and which bead removes it or why
#           it stays
#
# This list only shrinks. The remediation beads of the FIPS epic
# (midsommar-clean-8dy7) delete their entries as they land; the guard fails
# on an entry that no longer matches anything, so a fixed site cannot stay
# listed. Entries that stay are the dual-format readers (old formats every
# build must still read) and tests that build legacy fixtures. Do not add an
# entry for new code: use the approved primitive (crypto/pbkdf2, crypto/sha256,
# cipher.NewGCMWithRandomNonce, ...) instead.

# --- Password and secret hashing: bcrypt (PBKDF2 in FIPS mode, midsommar-clean-8dy7.14)
models/util.go                                   golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt  HashPassword/IsPasswordValid; bcrypt verify stays as the legacy reader, writer moves to PBKDF2 in .14
auth/auth.go                                     golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt  password set/reset hash bcrypt directly instead of models.HashPassword; .14
services/oauth_client_service.go                 golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt  OAuth client secret hash; .14
microgateway/internal/services/crypto_service.go golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt  microgateway HashSecret/VerifySecret; .14
microgateway/internal/services/crypto_service.go golang.org/x/crypto/pbkdf2  x/crypto PBKDF2 (outside the validated module) with a fixed salt; stdlib crypto/pbkdf2 in .14
api/auth_handlers_test.go                        golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt  test checks the stored hash is bcrypt; .14 makes it format-agnostic or keeps it as a legacy fixture
auth/auth_test.go                                golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt  test builds and checks bcrypt hashes; .14
auth/auth_lifecycle_test.go                      golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt  test seeds a bcrypt-hashed user; .14
services/oauth_client_service_test.go            golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt  test checks the stored OAuth secret is bcrypt; .14

# --- Secrets at rest (midsommar-clean-8dy7.10, .13)
secrets/models.go                                golang.org/x/crypto/scrypt  v2 secrets KDF; the v2 reader stays, FIPS-mode writes move to v3 PBKDF2 in .13
secrets/models.go                                cipher.NewGCM               AES-GCM with caller-supplied nonces; NewGCMWithRandomNonce in .10
secrets/models.go                                cipher.NewCFBDecrypter      legacy (pre-v2) secrets reader; stays so the re-encrypt sweep can read old values
secrets/gcm_test.go                              cipher.NewCFBEncrypter      test builds a legacy CFB secret fixture for the reader above

# --- Microgateway and hub->edge snapshot (midsommar-clean-8dy7.10, .15)
microgateway/internal/services/crypto_service.go cipher.NewGCM               microgateway secret encryption with caller nonces; NewGCMWithRandomNonce in .10
grpc/control_server.go                           cipher.NewGCM               deterministic HMAC-derived snapshot nonce for the sync checksum; capability-gated change in .15
grpc/snapshot_encryption_test.go                 cipher.NewGCM               test decrypts a snapshot the way the microgateway does; follows grpc/control_server.go in .10/.15

# --- Tests outside the remediation beads
pkg/agenttrace/staging_test.go                   cipher.NewGCM               test Sealer with a random nonce prefix; NewGCMWithRandomNonce would make it strict-mode clean (make test-fips, .12)

# --- Vendored and enterprise code
third_party/gorm.io/gorm/schema/naming.go        crypto/sha1                 upstream gorm (never edited by hand) hashes over-long index names with SHA-1; fails under fips140=only only for names over 64 chars
enterprise/features/agenttracing/keys/keys.go    cipher.NewGCM               agent tracing payload sealing (enterprise); covered by the enterprise crypto audit, .17
